  "soft": 0.0,
  "question": "Does a Rest API endpoint exist for enabling the dependency graph on a per repo basis?\nSelect Topic Area\nQuestion\nI'm trying to enable the dependency graph on a per repo basis, rather then at a global org or enterprise level. I can't seem to see it in the repo settings when I call is this not possible via the rest API? Thanks!",
  "task_description": "Does a Rest API endpoint exist for enabling the dependency graph on a per repo basis?\nSelect Topic Area\nQuestion\nI'm trying to enable the dependency graph on a per repo basis, rather then at a global org or enterprise level. I can't seem to see it in the repo settings when I call is this not possible via the rest API? Thanks!",
  "task_type": "single_page_section",
  "intent_category": "troubleshooting",
  "graph_opportunity": false,
  "predicted_answer": "No. There’s no REST API to toggle (enable/disable) the dependency graph per repository. The docs show enabling is done via the repository’s Security & analysis (Settings) UI (or via the enterprise management console / administrative shell for GHES), while the REST API surfaces endpoints for submitting dependency data to the dependency graph (not for turning the feature on/off).",
